## Django Forms Guidelines

### Form Types

- Use Django's form and model form classes for form handling and validation
- Create custom forms for complex validation logic
- Use ModelForm for model-based forms
- Implement inline formsets for related models

### Validation

- Use Django's validation framework to validate form and model data
- Implement custom validators for business logic
- Use clean() methods for field-level validation
- Implement clean() method for form-level validation
- Handle validation errors gracefully

### Business Logic

- Keep business logic in models and forms; keep views light and focused on request handling
- Implement form processing logic in forms when appropriate
- Use form methods for data transformation
- Handle file uploads in forms properly

### Security

- Always use CSRF protection for forms
- Validate and sanitize all user inputs
- Implement proper file upload validation
- Use Django's built-in security features

### User Experience

- Provide clear error messages
- Implement proper form styling and layout
- Use Django's form widgets appropriately
- Handle form submission states (loading, success, error)
